From fba9facb967d51f85368abbd5ad323363d22d19e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 07:24:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix booking creation crash, wire up Google Calendar sync, add
 missing dispute/admin endpoints

- bookings.js: fix ReferenceError where clientName was used before its
  const declaration, causing every booking creation to 500. Move Google
  Calendar helper functions to module scope (they were pasted mid-handler
  and never actually called). Wire up calendar event creation on booking
  and cancellation on cancel/status-change.
- db/pool.js: auto-create calendar_tokens table and appointments.calendar_event_id
  column on startup (previously calendar-auth.js queried a table that was
  never created anywhere). Also auto-run the shareholder-features migration
  (banners, disputes, messages, newsletter_subscribers, push_tokens,
  verification_documents) on every boot instead of leaving it as a
  manual-only script nothing ever called.
- migrations/add-shareholder-features.js: refactor into an idempotent,
  exported function usable both standalone and from pool.js's startup hook.
- sql/schema.sql: add calendar_event_id column and calendar_tokens table
  so a fresh install has them from the start.
- routes/admin.js: add bulk-reject providers endpoint (previously only
  bulk-approve and bulk-delete existed).
- routes/disputes.js: add GET/POST /:id/messages so client, provider, and
  admin can communicate within a dispute thread (dispute_messages table
  existed but had no routes).
